`getClusterTitleWidth` is a synchronous function, but `createLabel` is `async` and returns a Promise. Without `await`, `label` is a Promise object — `elem.node().appendChild(label)` will throw a TypeError ('parameter 1 is not of type Node'), and `label.getBBox()` will throw because Promises have no `getBBox` method. The function must be declared `async` and the call must use `await`:

```js
export const getClusterTitleWidth = async (elem, node) => {
  const label = await createLabel(node.label, node.labelStyle, undefined, true, false, node.width);
  ...
};
```

`getConfig()` is called twice in `setupImage` — once to check whether `fontSize` is set, and again to read it. `setupImage` is invoked for every image in a label (potentially inside `Promise.all` over many images). Cache the result before the conditional:

```ts
const config = getConfig();
const bodyFontSize = config.fontSize ?? window.getComputedStyle(document.body).fontSize;
```
This also lets you replace the `? :` ternary with a cleaner `??` fallback, since the only falsy value worth guarding is `undefined`/`null`.
